     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div><br></div><div>I have a simple SEM model:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><pre style=\"margin-bottom:20px;padding:6px 10px;border:1px solid rgb(214,214,214);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:14px;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:21px;color:rgb(10,10,10);overflow:auto;border-radius:3px\"><code style=\"border-width:medium;border-style:none;font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;border-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">model </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:bold;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(51,102,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(51,102,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">   # latent variables</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(51,102,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">     L1 =~ x1 + x2 + x3</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(51,102,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">     L2 =~ x4 + x5 + x6</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\"><br><br></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(51,102,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">   # regression</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(51,102,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">     L1 ~ L2</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-weight:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;color:rgb(51,102,51)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;</span></span></code></pre></div></code></div><br>So far so good. Now I would like to estimate the parameter for a quadratic relationship; Explicitly, I would like to have this regression:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">L1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> poly</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">L2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> <br><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">#or</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br>L1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> L2 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> I</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">L2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">^</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><font color=\"#000000\"></font></code></div><br>However, this syntax does not work in lavaan. How I can do that using the lavaan syntax?</div><div><br></div><div>My workaround would be to square the indicator variabales x4, x5, x6, but that seems a bit inelegant and I am also not completely sure whether this is equivalent.</div><div><br></div><div>Any help is appreciated!</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,<br>Jonas</div></div>"
    ]
